From 1bcad72935e58f3f857132c23a456b4b1402c69e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 02:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08133/11362] [outer-loop] Apply verified adversarial
 corrections to the ARC generation trilogy

Three hostile reviews landed against the identity census, the induce-prompt
audit and the generation ablation. Each correction was independently
re-derived from the runs' own cells before being applied; none was taken on
the reviewer's word. Corrigenda are append-only -- prior numbers preserved
beside their corrections, never replaced.

UPHELD AND MATERIAL:

* Ablation CONCLUSION retracted. The "the binding constraint is the metric's
  all-or-nothing shape" reinterpretation loses both legs. Leg 1: a control
  that was never run -- identity through distance-to-exact reaches within 2
  cells on 17/20 games and is tied-or-better than the induced engine on 208
  of 225, so "engines are near-miss machines, not identity machines" is
  false. Leg 2: the 1-cell HUD stratum lives on fresh (32.7% of 3346 rows),
  not on tail (0 of 70), and the record's null sits on tail. The NULL itself
  is untouched and stands as the whole result.

* Prompt-audit "NOT CLOSE TO BINDING" withdrawn. Every window came from a
  hardcoded WINDOW_K=12 dev constant; the live buffer is 25 (median of the
  agent's own logged transition_count) and _active_transitions() is uncapped.
  Re-rendered the shipped prompt at n=25 through the live GGUF vocab: sparse
  exploration-like buffers max at 11,114 tokens (68%), but the densest-25
  bound puts 3 of 20 games OVER the 16,384 ceiling (lp85 167%, bp35 152%,
  cn04 103%). Truncation is reachable on the live path and was never measured
  there. The reviewer's own 131% extrapolation is corrected in turn -- a
  linear per-transition marginal is unsound on an RLE-delta-encoded block.

* Rule-of-three denominator: lead with 3/14, not 3/20. Zero was observed only
  in the clean n>=3 population; the 20-game population contains successes.

* distance_to_exact population is 296, not 293 -- three shape-mismatch drops
  were undeclared, and they are the worst units, so the censoring ran in the
  flattering direction.

Also: live-store identity is 29.2% not 3.7% (the artifact was right, the prose
summary was wrong); "median 2 of 7 actions" downgraded from headline to
caveated body observation (it is a banked-solution-route artifact); five
numeric corrections to the ablation report; substantive-stratum min reachable
p restated at 7 clusters (0.015625, not 0.00390625).

New verifier gap logged: change_accuracy's denominator is engine-dependent --
a raising engine is scored only on rows it survives, so raising on hard rows
inflates the metric. Cannot manufacture the current null (it only inflates,
and the clean max is 0.0) but becomes load-bearing the moment any arm reports
a non-zero.

No default flipped, no prompt edited, no behavioural claim made. Evidence
dirs read-only throughout.

